Subject: [PATCH] ui/dbus: zero copy for the D-Bus display; ui: the layout of a guest dma-buf, shared

On top of 0006 (2026-10-03):

- ui/dmabuf-layout.c: the amdgpu layout code of the SDL window, shared.  A
  guest buffer's modifier (and DCC planes, unchecked) as the kernel derives
  it from the buffer's metadata; the GPU's pipe and packer bits from the
  consumer's modifier list, or without one from QEMU's own EGL display (the
  same GPU).  The SDL swapchain uses it with the compositor's list.
- D-Bus zero copy, for a client that lists the new
  org.qemu.Display1.Listener.Unix.ZeroCopy (with AsyncUpdate and
  ScanoutDMABUF2): ScanoutDMABUF2 carries the buffer's real layout when the
  guest fences its flushes, DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID otherwise (copy it); each
  UpdateDMABUF marks its buffer held by the client (token: the dma-buf's
  inode) and holds the guest's flush while the client still holds the buffer
  updated before (graphic_hw_gl_flush_pending); the client gives buffers back
  with the new Presentation.Released(token), and says when its frames go to
  the screen as they are with Presentation.ZeroCopy(on) (the zero-copy swap
  target); a client that goes away releases everything.  Traces dbus_zc_*.
  The client side is in dbus-display/ (attaches the guest's buffer to its
  surface 1:1, releases after the compositor's reads, after copies, or at
  once for skipped frames).

Measured on a 4K 240 Hz screen (full screen top-level client): key to screen
11.75 / 13.45 ms, a continuous drag's window stops 10.1 ms after the pointer,
window operations 10.65 repeats/s, against 12.6 / 14.15, 11.15 and 13.6 when
the client copies; the frames need a 1 ms longer swap target than the SDL
window's (host/run-vm.sh adds it for VM_DISPLAY=dbus).

Not committed in the fork yet; generated with diff on top of 0001-0006.

